kubeos-dashboard (0.1.0-16) trixie; urgency=medium

  * The "Apps" menu entry in 0.1.0-15 was a dead label: it appeared in the sidebar and clicking it
    did nothing (user: "it is like dummy button"). Cause: `registerSidebarEntry` was called without
    a `url`, and an entry that claims a `name` nothing else uses but carries no `url` is rendered as
    a GROUP heading, not a link. It now passes `url: '/kubeos-apps'` (plus `parent: null`), which is
    what every other KubeOS page does - `nfs.tsx`, `snapshots.tsx`, `rebalance.tsx` all pass it, and
    the only entries that legitimately omit it are groups whose children carry one ("Disks").
    Found by the user, not by me: the Helm endpoints were verified with curl but the page was never
    rendered in a browser, which is the one check that would have caught it. It is now checked that
    way - a headless browser logs into the dashboard, clicks "Apps" in the sidebar, and the release
    table is read back from the DOM.
  * Nothing else changed: same read-only page, same `/helm/*` endpoints, same release identity.

